<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">lenses</ansi>

Some rooms of the Obelisk hold a lens table: thirty-six lenses in six rows
of six, all turned face down. Only someone who can read the Obelisk's round
marks can make sense of one.

Every lens is tuned to a frequency, and every frequency appears twice. Turn
two lenses: if they agree, the light between them clicks into place and both
stay up. If they do not, both turn face down again. Lock every pair to open
the way the table holds shut.

The table forgives only so many mistakes. When they run out, every lens turns
face down again, even the pairs you locked, and the table forgives fewer the
next time. When its patience runs out for the last time it goes dark for
good, and you will have to find another table in another room.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">1c</ansi>
  Turn the lens in row 1, column c.

  <ansi fg="command">1c 4e</ansi>
  Turn two lenses at once.

  <ansi fg="command">look table</ansi>
  See the table as it stands.
